<title>INDIA: India RBI set interest rate cap on export credit.</title>
<headline>India RBI set interest rate cap on export credit.</headline>
<dateline>BOMBAY 1996-10-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Reserve Bank of India (RBI) said on Saturday that it had set an interest rate cap of 15 percent per annum on export credit.</p>
<p>The new rule is effective from October 21, 1996.</p>
<p>This measure was announced in the RBI's monetary policy for the second half of 1996/97.</p>
<p>Banks, which were earlier free to determine interest rates on export credit beyond 90 days, could now charge a maximum of only 15 percent per annum, it said.</p>
<p>The interest rates on export credit up to 90 days remains unchanged at 13 percent per annum, the RBI said.</p>
<p>-- Bombay newsroom +91-22-265 9000</p>
</text>
